## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Pub/Sub triggers, Cloud Functions, BigQuery streaming inserts, and idempotency.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub triggers and Cloud Functions
- Idempotent writes using BigQuery insertId
- Date-partitioned tables for perf
- Minimal IAM and retry strategies
- Basic test plan with duplicates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cloud Function (Pub/Sub trigger) schematic
const {BigQuery} = require('@google-cloud/bigquery');
const bigquery = new BigQuery();
exports.aggregateEvent = async (msg, context) => {
  const payload = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(msg.data, 'base64').toString());
  const eventId = payload.event_id;
  const userId = payload.user_id;
  const minute = new Date(payload.timestamp).toISOString().slice(0,16);
  const rows = [{insertId: eventId, user_id: userId, minute: minute}];
  await bigquery
    .dataset('analytics')
    .table('app_events_minutes')
    .insert(rows);
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotency in a CI environment?
- What changes would you make to handle out-of-order messages or late arrivals?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end data ingestion, validation, redaction, and end-of-day analytics using beginner-friendly GCP primitives, plus a focus on security and idempotency.

## Key Concepts

- Cloud Run HTTPS endpoints
- Pub/Sub integration
- Cloud Functions for validation and redaction
- Cloud Storage with date-based prefixes
- BigQuery nightly ETL
- Idempotency via insertId
- Minimal IAM bindings and testability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo Cloud Function outline
exports.validateAndRedact = (event, context) => {
  const lines = readLinesFromGCS(event);
  lines.forEach(l => {
    if (validate(l)) {
      const redacted = redactPII(l);
      writeToGCS(redacted);
    }
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotency for duplicate Pub/Sub messages?
